{"key":"mac c033 s0 guide","answer":{"rc":0,"stdout":"hydo 0.3.1: the guide built into this hydo. Its facts (the project format, the commands and\ntheir options, the fault kinds, the limits) are the ones this hydo has.\n\nTo onboard a project, follow the hydo-onboard skill (the process; it asks this guide for facts):\n\n  Claude Code     /plugin marketplace add kakoc/hydo\n                  /plugin install hydo-onboard@hydo        (updates come as plugin updates)\n  Codex, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Gemini CLI\n                  hydo skill install --agent codex|cursor|copilot|gemini [--user]\n                  hydo skill update                        (fetches the newest skill release)\n  any other tool  tell it: \"run `hydo guide skill` and follow it\"\n\nStart with `hydo guide workflow`. The topics:\n\n  hydo guide capabilities       What works where\n  hydo guide checks             Checks in hydo/checks/\n  hydo guide ci                 Running hydo in continuous integration (hydo ci run)\n  hydo guide composer           The test composer: commands in hydo/workload/\n  hydo guide error-logs         Error logs as findings\n  hydo guide faults             Faults, knobs, and exploring\n  hydo guide flaky-tests        Flaky tests: run a test program under hydo\n  hydo guide hazards            Determinism and environment hazards\n  hydo guide inspect            Why a run failed, and looking inside a run without changing it\n  hydo guide invariant-patterns Check patterns\n  hydo guide manifest           the project format explained: hydo.yaml and the hydo/ folder (MANIFEST.md)\n  hydo guide messages           Messaging checks (queues, logs, publish-subscribe)\n  hydo guide numbered-steps     The numbered-steps workload (`workload.run`)\n  hydo guide outside-services   Outside services, protocol faults, and generated gRPC drivers\n  hydo guide schema             the project format's JSON Schema (format 1, hydo/schema/project-v1.json)\n  hydo guide sdks               SDKs: assertions inside the programs, and tests written in code\n  hydo guide services           Services and guest settings\n  hydo guide skill              the onboarding skill's SKILL.md (the process), for a tool without skills\n  hydo guide workflow           Onboarding with this hydo: the commands and the files\n  hydo guide workloads          Ready-made workloads and checks (SQL systems, and business rules)\n  hydo guide examples/<file>    a file of the examples (start with examples/example-redis-composed/README.md)\n","stderr":"","files":{"home/":""}}}
